{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdLogTLUP1FyN2BXMMQMW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-286 is complete. Committed as `b988c18` on train branch `llm/train/p0-g3-WI-286-9253` with the correct worker trailers (WI/Train/Base), parented on the integration base.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nA dispatcher train worktree has no `.venv` of its own, so a bare `python`/`pytest` there resolved whatever was ambient on PATH. I confirmed the bug **live in this very worktree**: ambient `python` = **3.8.10** (below the 3.11 floor), while the main repo's shared venv = **3.11.9**. A below-floor idiom would pass locally and only fail in CI, and the pinned dev tools could be absent.\n\n## The fix (shared root `.venv` by absolute path)\n\n- **`agent_common.py`** — `venv_python` / `harness_python` / `interpreter_version` helpers + `MIN_PYTHON = (3, 11)`; `_declared_test_command` gained an explicit `{py}` arg (default unchanged, so WI-285 stays intact).\n- **`agent_dispatch.py`** — `_activate_root_venv` points the dispatcher *and every child it spawns* (worker agent sessions, the pre-commit floor, `./scripts/check.sh`, the integrator's staging commits) at the root `.venv`; `_run_combined_bar`'s `{py}` resolves to that same venv; `_harness_floor_failures` folds into the existing preflight gate (joined with `+`, so `dispatch_run`'s complexity baseline is unmoved) and refuses a below-floor `.venv`/ambient/unrunnable interpreter **before any worker or bar runs**.\n- **Decision recorded** in the spec Resolution: shared root venv (not per-worktree — the stdlib-only kit needs pinned tools only for tests); ships downstream verbatim, no migration.\n\n## Verification (all under the main venv 3.11.9)\n\n- **Full suite: 1426 passed, 5 skipped** (`-m pytest -q -n auto`, ~6 min).\n- New tests: helper unit tests, floor-refusal at unit **and** end-to-end (`test_dispatcher_refuses_a_below_floor_harness_interpreter`), and `_run_combined_bar` runs under the root venv.\n- Pre-commit floor green (arch-map regenerated for 3 new public symbols; ruff format + lint clean; complexity ratchet unmoved; `agent_dispatch.py` size baseline re-stamped 3538 → 3614 with a reviewed reason).\n\nA telling detail from the commit: the worktree's pre-commit hook resolved ambient `python3` (3.12) and **skipped the format step because ruff wasn't importable there** — exactly the ambient-resolution gap this WI closes (a real dispatcher run now activates the venv, so the hook gets ruff and format actually runs).\n\nLeft for the integrator per the worker contract: the `done` row-flip, spec archive, and root-artifact regeneration on the composed tree."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1108,"cache_read_input_tokens":273585,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1108},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90606481-3613-403f-a6ad-871cad87425e","uuid":"6234706d-0018-4b5c-bd50-a3e491c0c467","request_id":"req_011CdLogRe2GsUd9U41wfHQh"}
